# scripts/install/EXPECTED_RELEASE — LivOS release pin (Phase 311-04, UPDSAFE-02)
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   A single "pin line" naming the release this repo tree belongs to. update.sh's
#   livos_verify_fetched_ref() reads it out of the freshly-cloned release tree and
#   compares the resolved commit against the fetched HEAD.
#
# FORMAT (consumed by update.sh:  grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)' | head -1 | tr -d '[:space:]')
#   * Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   * The FIRST non-comment line is the pin.
#   * Use the FULL  refs/tags/<tag>  form. A refs/tags/<tag> line is resolved to a
#     commit via  git rev-parse "<tag>^{commit}"  INSIDE the cloned tree, then
#     compared to the fetched HEAD SHA. Because boxes clone a release BY that same
#     tag, HEAD == the tag's commit == what refs/tags/<tag> resolves to → a
#     self-consistent match.
#
# WARN-ONLY (Phase 311) — NOT enforcement
#   In Phase 311 a pin mismatch is WARN-ONLY: livos_verify_fetched_ref() logs a
#   SIGNATURE-WARN, records a signature_verification verdict into the update-history
#   JSON, and PROCEEDS — it never aborts an update. The fail-closed flip (refuse to
#   deploy on mismatch) is Phase 312, a strictly LATER release, gated on one full
#   release cycle of this warn-only telemetry. Do NOT add enforcement here or in the
#   verify function as part of Phase 311.
#
