#   had two structural causes, both closed in `2d8302be`:
#     (a) Snapshot scope. VM disk images (${dataDirectory}/vm-data) are tens of GB
#         and every VM boot rewrites blocks throughout them — the single worst
#         thing to snapshot hourly onto the same disk. Now excluded BY DEFAULT via
#         a visible, reversible toggle beside the existing scope switches (never a
#         hidden rule: silently dropping someone's VM from their backups would be
#         the exact dishonesty this milestone keeps removing). Browser-profile
#         caches under chrome-master are excluded unconditionally — pure
#         regenerable bulk, while Cookies/Login Data/Preferences stay in. Those
#         patterns are ANCHORED to the profile root; a depth-agnostic `Cache/`
