#         still write the disk to zero on the way through. A watchdog now polls
#         during any snapshot written to the system disk and kills kopia below 5%
#         free. Safe: kopia commits atomically, so the repo keeps its previous
#         snapshots and simply gains no new one; the run is marked failed and the
#         >24h alert fires. The 5% floor is deliberately BELOW the 15% pre-flight
#         floor (crossing 15% mid-run is normal for a large first snapshot), and
#         its failure mode is deliberately the OPPOSITE: an unreadable probe
#         mid-run does NOT abort, because the pre-flight already proved there was
#         room and aborting on a transient df hiccup would leave a flaky box never
#         completing a backup.
